        content: "ELIC is a React Native mobile app that teaches English to Thai speakers through role-play in realistic situations. Six scenarios each carry their own persona injected as a system prompt: hotel, restaurant, job interview, doctor visit, meeting new friends, and taxi; difficulty is a second axis, so the same scene can be played easy or hard. The model does not reply as plain text — it returns JSON that the app splits into three components: the chat bubble, a SpellingCorrection panel showing the original phrase, the corrected phrase and an explanation in both Thai and English, and a VocabularyTable of English/Thai/example sentence. The parser never trusts the model to send clean JSON: it strips code fences, takes the span from the first brace to the last, and falls back to rendering plain text so a malformed answer becomes an ordinary chat message instead of an error screen. Conversation memory is bounded: only the last 8 turns are sent as context, a conversation counts as long past 40 messages or roughly 6,000 characters, and beyond that older messages are dropped by an importance score computed from message length, presence of a question mark and extracted topic keywords, keeping the most recent 75% intact and restoring only high-scoring older messages. Two models are used on purpose: chat runs on typhoon-s-thaillm-8b-instruct via ThaiLLM (temperature 0.5, max_tokens 1024) because a Thai-tuned model explains mistakes in Thai far better, while the games use gemini-2.0-flash where speed matters more. Chat migrated off Gemini in May 2026. Latency work: streaming tokens brought the first token from 1,800 ms down to about 300 ms, which the README notes was the lesson carried into later RAG work. Text-to-speech has three paths: expo-speech on device, a FastAPI server (api/tts_server.py) using the Gemini Live voice API, and a Flask bridge (api/speech_server.py). Games include Word Game (model-judged words starting with a random letter), Translation (curated Thai sentences, 7 categories x 2 levels, model-scored), Match (English-Thai card matching in 60 seconds over a hand-built vocabulary of more than 1,400 words), and a live Rank/Scoreboard on Firebase Realtime Database. Auth is Firebase Auth with email/password and Google Sign-In, mirrored into AsyncStorage for instant startup. 13 screens, React Navigation 6, React Native 0.76.9, Expo SDK 52. APK builds run through EAS plus GitHub Actions. Timeline: first commit August 2024, games and scoreboard March-June 2025, UI rebuild October 2025, ThaiLLM migration May 2026. 48 commits, roughly 14,600 lines. MIT licensed. GitHub: https://github.com/watcharaponthod-code/elic",
