        title: "Project: trading — AlgoTrade, a full-stack algorithmic trading dashboard on Alpaca",
        content: "trading (AlgoTrade) is a full-stack algorithmic trading dashboard for paper and live trading through the Alpaca Markets API, deployed on Vercel with a live demo at trading-jet-iota.vercel.app. The auto-trader runs the strategy engine every minute through Vercel Cron Jobs, so no separate always-on server is needed; the README notes that the Vercel Hobby tier caps cron at daily, and recommends an external scheduler such as cron-job.org calling GET /api/cron/ai-trade hourly with a bearer CRON_SECRET header for hourly AI trading. Four strategies are implemented: momentum, mean reversion, statistical arbitrage and pairs trading, with crypto symbols BTC, ETH, SOL, AVAX and DOGE tradeable around the clock. Risk management covers a portfolio heat limit, a daily profit-and-loss cutoff and stale order cleanup. The dashboard shows a portfolio equity chart, P&L history and open positions in real time, and every signal and trade execution is pushed to Telegram through a bot. The stack by layer is Next.js 16 with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4 and Recharts on the frontend; Next.js API routes running serverless on the backend; Vercel Cron Jobs for scheduling; the Alpaca Markets API as broker for both paper and live; Neon PostgreSQL in production with SQLite locally; Vercel free tier for hosting; and the Telegram Bot API for notifications. The API surface in app/api includes account, auto-trader, crypto-trader, market, orders, portfolio, positions, signals, snapshots, stat-arb, strategy, trade, a telegram/webhook endpoint, database-backed routes db-signals, db-snapshots, db-strategies and db-trades, and three cron entry points: cron/trade, cron/crypto and cron/ai-trade. Core logic lives in lib/: alpaca.ts for the broker client, strategy.ts and enhanced-strategy.ts for signal generation, advanced-indicators.ts for technical indicators, stat-arb-engine.ts for statistical arbitrage, risk-manager.ts for position and exposure limits, db.ts and migrate.ts for persistence, telegram-bot.ts for alerts and firebase.ts. UI components under components/trading include auto-trader-panel, order-form, orders-table, pnl-chart, portfolio-chart, positions-table, price-chart, stat-arb-panel, stat-card, strategy-panel and watchlist-panel, on top of a shadcn-style component library. Configuration is through environment variables ALPACA_API_KEY, ALPACA_API_SECRET, ALPACA_BASE_URL, DATABASE_URL, CRON_SECRET, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_IDS. Docker and Dockerfile.worker plus PM2 ecosystem configs exist for non-serverless deployment. The README reports no backtest results or live performance figures. GitHub: https://github.com/watcharaponthod-code/trading",
